--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 1095's report-only temporary-candidate attribution is required to
preserve task ownership evidence at roar. On 2026-10-19 the full Codex report
timed out after 90 seconds without output. A bounded diagnosis measured
candidate scanning at 13.941 seconds and history enumeration at 0.413 seconds;
the attribution stage was still running after the second 25-second probe, with
about 10.6 seconds of that probe available after the preceding stages. This is
a lower bound, not a completion-time measurement. The durable capture is
`memory/journal/2026/2026-10-19-tmp-report-timeout-diagnosis.md`.

The report currently builds a global session-parent graph and performs
candidate-specific checks. Any optimization must preserve attribution scope
and its distinctions between mentions, verified creation calls, and inferred
test provenance.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Add a read-only profiling harness outside the production report path,
  at `scripts/profile_tmp_report.py`, with a hard wall-clock cap and per-stage
  elapsed times and counts for candidate scan, history enumeration,
  attribution, references, and inference.
- [x] Emit aggregate counts and durations only; do not emit history text,
  commands, candidate paths, or secret-bearing content.
- [x] Keep the global session-parent graph required for descendant attribution;
  document and verify any narrower citation or command scan.
- [x] Compare old and proposed behavior on a bounded fixture covering parent
  and child sessions, the excluded reporting session, mtime cutoffs, and
  ambiguous commands; preserve the distinction between mentions, verified
  creation, and test-source inference.
- [x] Measure references and test-source inference independently before
  assigning them any share of the original 90-second timeout.
- [x] Keep probes read-only and make timeout or incomplete-stage status
  explicit.
- [x] Bound production history attribution to a configurable cooperative
  budget (20 seconds by default; zero requests exhaustive scanning). On a
  partial scan, retain positive evidence, report file coverage and mark missing
  attribution and Roar ancestry unknown rather than unattributed or complete.
- [x] Review the implementation and run the relevant checks before integrating
  with ticket 1095's remaining work.
